TechGear Product Catalog
Objective
Build a mini React application using react-router-dom that allows users to:
Browse products.
Filter products using Query Parameters (?category=...&maxPrice=...).
View specific product details using Dynamic Route Parameters (/product/:productId).
Starter Data
Create a file named productsData.js and paste the following array:
const PRODUCTS = [
  { id: '1', name: 'Wireless Headphones', category: 'audio', price: 150 },
  { id: '2', name: 'Bluetooth Speaker', category: 'audio', price: 80 },
  { id: '3', name: 'Mechanical Keyboard', category: 'peripherals', price: 120 },
  { id: '4', name: 'Ergonomic Mouse', category: 'peripherals', price: 60 },
  { id: '5', name: '4K Monitor', category: 'display', price: 350 },
];
Task Instructions
Requirement 1: Navigation Bar 
Create a persistent <nav> component at the top of the application using <Link>.
Include links to:
All Products: /products
Audio Only: /products?category=audio
Under $100: /products?maxPrice=100
Requirement 2: Product Catalog (/products) 
Create a ProductCatalog component rendered at /products using useSearchParams.
Read Parameters:
Extract category and maxPrice values from the URL query string.
Filter Products:
Filter the PRODUCTS array based on the active query parameter values.
Interactive Filter Controls:
Add a <select> dropdown for categories (audio, peripherals, display).
Add an <input type="number"> for maxPrice.
Updating either control must update the URL using setSearchParams().
Add a "Clear Filters" button that resets search parameters to /products.
Display List:
Render each matching product's name and price.
Attach a link to each item leading to /product/:productId.
Requirement 3: Product Details (/product/:productId) 
Create a ProductDetails component rendered at /product/:productId using useParams.
Read Dynamic Route:
Extract productId from the dynamic path segment.
Display Product:
Find and render the product details (Name, Price, Category, ID) matching productId.
If no match exists, display "Product not found!".
Back Navigation:
Add a <Link to="/products"> button to navigate back to the catalog.
Requirement 4: Verification Check 
Test your implementation against these manual scenarios:
Scenario A: Typing /product/103 in the browser bar renders the Mechanical Keyboard page directly.
Scenario B: Selecting "audio" from the dropdown updates the browser address bar to ?category=audio without a page refresh.
Scenario C: Reloading the page at /products?category=audio&maxPrice=100 preserves the filtered state automatically.
